n```tsv\n부동산업\t부동산업\t부동산 임대 및 공급업\n```","thinking":"Focusing on the employee count discrepancy between source data (real DB) and public data (Bizno/National Pension), I'll investigate the context of `899-01-00125`. This is a sole proprietorship, indicated by the \"01\" in the middle of the number. Sole proprietors lack a corporate registration number, explaining the blank field. Similarly, their financial year-end is usually blank, unlike registered corporations.\n\n\nThe business type is confirmed as \"비주거용 건물 임대업\" (Non-residential building leasing) based on the real DB and address, which aligns with the operation of leasing two units in a knowledge industry center. The employee count in the source data is listed as 3, but the business is a closed sole proprietorship. The most suitable approach would be to explain the validation rules and either keep the original count or note the closure in the remarks column.\n\n\nConfirmed \"폐업\" (closed) status from the provided data. Verified the address and postal code. I'm cross-referencing this information with the standard industry classification (KSIC) to ensure consistency within the dataset, specifically confirming the \"비주거용 건물 임대업\" (non-residential building leasing) designation. I am now matching data to the column headers in the spreadsheet, carefully mapping information from row 20419. I'm double-checking the column headers with those from row 20418 to eliminate discrepancies.\n\n\nThe current focus is on reconciling the provided data with the established TSV template and existing data. Examining the column definitions is critical to ensure accurate data mapping. Specifically, cross-referencing the input information with the standard column order ([작성자] [비고] [회사명] ... [업종_소]) is essential.\n\nI'm now identifying corresponding data points from the provided example (e.g., \"보연\" for \"회사명\") to their respective columns in the template. The goal is to accurately populate the remaining fields, address the inconsistencies, and address any anomalies, specifically the sole proprietorship designation.\n\n\nThe \"결산월\" field is blank for sole proprietors, and the business's industry classifications are \"부동산업\" (real estate) for the large and medium categories, and \"부동산 임대 및 공급업\" (real estate rental and supply) for the small category, respectively. The source data's employee count of 3 is accurate according to the original data, however, the business is closed. I will keep the original employee count and note \"폐업\" (closed) in the remarks.\n\n\n"}
